{:db/id "q-106608" :question/id #uuid "d04dc5b8-08a6-57d8-bded-d4e9790647ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-106608" :question/problem "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}=20?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{5{y}^{2}}{20}-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{20} & =\\frac{20}{20} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=\\sqrt{5}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6e4940d-fc80-563d-85a2-b83478cce6c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325821/field-1/ed2234e47c01521cbbd95bbc8c734350d1f8dec88e7e65a5af1239b780d0b7a0" :answer/id #uuid "9d08964a-2b5d-5a7f-9f2c-99c4f3e02cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\tan(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325821/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe95b6e-5e04-5baa-8274-00296ef1886e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325821/field-1/ed2234e47c01521cbbd95bbc8c734350d1f8dec88e7e65a5af1239b780d0b7a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-325821/field-1/ed2234e47c01521cbbd95bbc8c734350d1f8dec88e7e65a5af1239b780d0b7a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325821" :question/id #uuid "f683f444-563d-5b98-96a5-63779a59f5ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-325821" :question/problem "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2}=20$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{20}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{20} & =\\frac{20}{20} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325821/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6e4940d-fc80-563d-85a2-b83478cce6c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325821"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-89068"] :question/problem "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{25}=5$ and $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-325818/field-1/b0c61fcfef9eab8b93162a281bff415db7aebbb6c1093ce50111ba9ee81b6a2f" :answer/id #uuid "a78b2cc7-dc61-5dba-a08e-457a2b7b6a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325818/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "17e9a7de-9ac1-578a-abd7-725835ba3704" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325818/field-1/b0c61fcfef9eab8b93162a281bff415db7aebbb6c1093ce50111ba9ee81b6a2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-325818/field-1/b0c61fcfef9eab8b93162a281bff415db7aebbb6c1093ce50111ba9ee81b6a2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325818" :question/id #uuid "201a3946-c922-53a0-bacb-39155ab1c2e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-325818" :question/problem "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2}=40$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{5{y}^{2}}{40}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{40} & =\\frac{40}{40} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\sqrt{5}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325818/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6e4940d-fc80-563d-85a2-b83478cce6c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325849/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "eb9f22c3-74c4-5b8e-bc81-08a88cfb90cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325849/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "872d4ecb-c1d8-53f2-87d5-d367cd2be66a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325849/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-325849/field-1/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325849/field-2/1e9a76cebdc0d8731b28e39cd38fc3f64898b0cbe44af30a011d52171ca75dc3" :answer/id #uuid "f2117b3c-2428-544d-9df7-c0c99926ac4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325849/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d84a12cf-ca2d-55a7-b2c1-bd05ace5fe9b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325849/field-2/1e9a76cebdc0d8731b28e39cd38fc3f64898b0cbe44af30a011d52171ca75dc3" :answer-field/choices ["q-325849/field-2/1e9a76cebdc0d8731b28e39cd38fc3f64898b0cbe44af30a011d52171ca75dc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325849" :question/id #uuid "fab15ed8-d110-5c0a-bb37-2091717ed4f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-325849" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/e2c0bc639d03c94056b07ce1cc42976b88494f312e318199cef73043bc711c74.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,$\n$y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,3)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325849/field-1" "q-325849/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection/b0d902a9e5e965810e77bd5577c3937ca8b72ccd5e64d9a6b6f734cd3413227e" :answer/id #uuid "1afbf06a-297c-5ee2-b9d1-9b797167ac6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection/4e200d4f22df8cb68ce266a1873ff902715e0a11cb6bc297e99f08b371934cd8" :answer/id #uuid "34a5a16f-5e2a-501c-9c05-7d8e3588051a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection/63480ceb1882d5bfb5753f044c7340eb55a3163de2259641878e5c182b0be3de" :answer/id #uuid "66dfbd48-73e4-5586-9b95-f706d1df1511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection/eda6696a18f7e0f4340c36035a2e5ccf4f4a18e3fe0d731385e5fea2ead9cd37" :answer/id #uuid "d162ca6b-2bb8-5578-b8c5-dd0c935d07e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection/a67b4bfadf4f39a9dac5377a4e300cc58c80326e193a6256d2e35796f3d6d117" :answer/id #uuid "581020ee-018e-5525-a0a2-1b9c570127dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a424228-f16e-5293-ae53-ee24b73245ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106617/selection/4e200d4f22df8cb68ce266a1873ff902715e0a11cb6bc297e99f08b371934cd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-106617/selection/b0d902a9e5e965810e77bd5577c3937ca8b72ccd5e64d9a6b6f734cd3413227e" "q-106617/selection/4e200d4f22df8cb68ce266a1873ff902715e0a11cb6bc297e99f08b371934cd8" "q-106617/selection/63480ceb1882d5bfb5753f044c7340eb55a3163de2259641878e5c182b0be3de" "q-106617/selection/eda6696a18f7e0f4340c36035a2e5ccf4f4a18e3fe0d731385e5fea2ead9cd37" "q-106617/selection/a67b4bfadf4f39a9dac5377a4e300cc58c80326e193a6256d2e35796f3d6d117"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106617" :question/id #uuid "9fa09b3c-df1e-55fe-b2c4-e14f1cc9a066" :question/math-academy-id "q-106617" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/6044a47f621612d56138893be089f48a2d2a7060c13d044086154ab7892fac38.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,1)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection/bd1e7b656af04b968d39157de766c09919229c4a15172d11e0850c5868a5862e" :answer/id #uuid "24880b86-4cae-5b70-a80e-144502a0e917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection/9579956d4e72962b5b0c48861ff98704f034d23c0b1d4a89715e4ae84b99ba2a" :answer/id #uuid "e3f43754-8c54-53af-9947-b183e5faae90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection/b4106d02fb60260c826694c9f714926c77820ca15b7483865f868963b535f460" :answer/id #uuid "588169c4-5db7-5588-8399-debaa184ee9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection/e6e68186f004ca709432a8ed171da3081ab393270e490405fa3c05ccc918e7da" :answer/id #uuid "3efa7b90-80b1-5171-83e9-23663b93924d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=9\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection/49a3984b8858a722d9a34c5666ea7a5561fd010a49b3b1e94e74c348363811a7" :answer/id #uuid "0278f54d-318a-5abd-908b-a4eccdb8622e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0325bf50-412d-5f7e-97f1-96cdf824d0c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106620/selection/49a3984b8858a722d9a34c5666ea7a5561fd010a49b3b1e94e74c348363811a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-106620/selection/bd1e7b656af04b968d39157de766c09919229c4a15172d11e0850c5868a5862e" "q-106620/selection/9579956d4e72962b5b0c48861ff98704f034d23c0b1d4a89715e4ae84b99ba2a" "q-106620/selection/b4106d02fb60260c826694c9f714926c77820ca15b7483865f868963b535f460" "q-106620/selection/e6e68186f004ca709432a8ed171da3081ab393270e490405fa3c05ccc918e7da" "q-106620/selection/49a3984b8858a722d9a34c5666ea7a5561fd010a49b3b1e94e74c348363811a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106620" :question/id #uuid "fc8cdff2-ffdf-55ed-95c0-18e8793dab2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106620" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/e2203c195dbcd9ae474f5d00f00e81d63ec6527c0367e96a8a7520522c967265.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-3)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106620/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106620"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection/779ecd82ca2696247eeb3e3943f1d1fd22384cf0926ef47a645af803feb685cf" :answer/id #uuid "c1cc953a-b2c5-5cf1-a42e-eb152267c1b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection/51d1d5642592e8d61a86a3b33429d2146a9d840a4768486da6d73a0cc9c3bfb9" :answer/id #uuid "4134906b-ade5-585e-9eed-8a3ae86cf7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection/8e470aa98d7fee7429ef22f65372397999d6e66c54d3f317279b932706945e24" :answer/id #uuid "8be63e8e-43ea-5a46-bdfb-1cffe551e7ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection/5b50d84bfb9f66f7e3195ae586eb0da1f74e7fb704de6af53db3f3345566ab03" :answer/id #uuid "2daadef7-7b6d-5921-a1b7-07cb6e37173c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection/c043cbee521d6f323b7295264cd6aac2c50840168e6e2fe48dfac7566901c54b" :answer/id #uuid "bfaf5efa-9ea0-5e87-a861-af9ff6bb9942" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f87579f-d2ff-556b-9b50-773ad175d759" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106615/selection/c043cbee521d6f323b7295264cd6aac2c50840168e6e2fe48dfac7566901c54b" :answer-field/choices ["q-106615/selection/779ecd82ca2696247eeb3e3943f1d1fd22384cf0926ef47a645af803feb685cf" "q-106615/selection/51d1d5642592e8d61a86a3b33429d2146a9d840a4768486da6d73a0cc9c3bfb9" "q-106615/selection/8e470aa98d7fee7429ef22f65372397999d6e66c54d3f317279b932706945e24" "q-106615/selection/5b50d84bfb9f66f7e3195ae586eb0da1f74e7fb704de6af53db3f3345566ab03" "q-106615/selection/c043cbee521d6f323b7295264cd6aac2c50840168e6e2fe48dfac7566901c54b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106615" :question/id #uuid "fabfdbc4-b695-5ce4-bd18-c77c662dc09c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106615" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/09873582f6b52b28ca5223605479cc98df4ead7cf0940ea4cadfa66301694911.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,\\sqrt{3})$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{b} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275792/field-1/7a019166d53f8f445cfca04bbbb5d9fea414f91656d4091feae12bd71715d58a" :answer/id #uuid "ff92f23b-c5fc-5780-9d67-12a377e8284b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\tan(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275792/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe5368bc-e1e1-50eb-9eac-2b5d739feafb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275792/field-1/7a019166d53f8f445cfca04bbbb5d9fea414f91656d4091feae12bd71715d58a" :answer-field/choices ["q-275792/field-1/7a019166d53f8f445cfca04bbbb5d9fea414f91656d4091feae12bd71715d58a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275792/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c87358ea-65e8-5e8e-8430-96d83b5ed9a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275792/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a71d719c-bae2-5673-af1c-680218afe7d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275792/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-275792/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275792" :question/id #uuid "5c73b5f1-13f8-5d58-9924-2732adfaffbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275792" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/20138a518801a1bac0a76303a86d6ca4b2fe289f5dae230517730f7398de3945.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,4)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=4.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275792/field-1" "q-275792/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275792"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275794/field-1/7a558a90b2ddf9a7c2bff1523b6e656914fdba10a9e72f6b7f1a48a4ec330279" :answer/id #uuid "6e3fb98d-0aa1-59f4-99f7-7dd5f4551cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y^2}{4}-\\frac{x^2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275794/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "218ac79c-d158-5f2b-a6e7-0600ffef1184" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275794/field-1/7a558a90b2ddf9a7c2bff1523b6e656914fdba10a9e72f6b7f1a48a4ec330279" :answer-field/choices ["q-275794/field-1/7a558a90b2ddf9a7c2bff1523b6e656914fdba10a9e72f6b7f1a48a4ec330279"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275794" :question/id #uuid "3ae69cc2-2076-5c1c-92eb-0c5855f63441" :question/math-academy-id "q-275794" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275794/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494f9793-de3b-5a0e-8ee9-38a8bad0f970"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275794"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325905/field-1/d88f7de58082c51d215112bc2f47e71229ea0859153f50a7cf2455faae8e50b7" :answer/id #uuid "7ee5f6e0-89ce-5954-98b4-0653b10a808a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y^2}{24}-\\frac{x^2}{45}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325905/field-1/e1e73102836277c437d235291dbbf56a4c37ecb7f7cc0eadc42c07b471f7a109" :answer/id #uuid "f3958474-4370-572d-8659-d028ef6cac29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y^2}{24}+\\frac{x^2}{45}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325905/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b0f1d42-9a59-58e8-b31c-57af64087727" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325905/field-1/d88f7de58082c51d215112bc2f47e71229ea0859153f50a7cf2455faae8e50b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-325905/field-1/d88f7de58082c51d215112bc2f47e71229ea0859153f50a7cf2455faae8e50b7" "q-325905/field-1/e1e73102836277c437d235291dbbf56a4c37ecb7f7cc0eadc42c07b471f7a109"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325905" :question/id #uuid "ea996889-9e23-5a96-b5ed-4f94b6d927c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-325905" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant–tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{45} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{6}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{24} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{45}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{45} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325905/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "494f9793-de3b-5a0e-8ee9-38a8bad0f970"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325905"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection/9b18f4aa4ca8076362df6e4f35a55a45089a7c57e7b0610433415513191ea892" :answer/id #uuid "952863ea-7c16-5ce0-8530-8271bc15b34c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection/854d6742ffdfb42914756668b0bd07bb1900be4c948c150457d3ce28305840c9" :answer/id #uuid "7eceaa67-e4ff-52bc-9ade-65aa1f009f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection/ee58113f2a373e41e2964a5ee1bf0f361d78705a29d3fc817c1185d44f5d8a47" :answer/id #uuid "6970ed7d-90dc-5363-a471-850dc615ecf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection/a699a1bc208ef2e6f4464b205899fb5bc1df6a553cd007abf2312aed6f19c081" :answer/id #uuid "4a625f29-b3b1-5f2f-a1e1-5e29b15a2f6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection/635f9e358f8dce2092fbb04c0795233f377d024a4a998e370e166e25c5b76ff5" :answer/id #uuid "61998645-3741-53ab-8927-a497ce1cbd5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106671/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a321b7b9-3f1e-5e55-8686-a575a39afa87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106671/selection